dfmea.md:

# Design FMEA (qualitative, simulation-signal based) — VBF-T5R1NOCEILING-DFMEA-01
Annotate: qualitative version, based on simulation signals; ratings S/O are qualitative three-level (high/medium/low) from the magnitude of the simulated value vs threshold; RPN = S x O simplified qualitative matrix; process/supplier failures N/A (beyond pure simulation boundary).

| Failure mode | Failure cause | Simulation signal | S | O | Mitigation (design-side) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Li plating during 4C fast charge | end-of-charge anode surface potential < 0 V (empty-anode polarization) | anode_potential_v min +0.0212 V (margin 21 mV) | high | low | implemented: area x1.5 dilution, 1.0 um anode particles, transport overrides; fallback R4B validated |
| Thermal runaway risk (excessive temperature rise) | 4C charge heat generation exceeds cooling | T_max 320.36 K vs 333.15 K (margin 12.8 K) | high | low | implemented: h=200 W/m2/K cooling, thin stack |
| Electrolyte oxidative decomposition | high cathode potential at charge ceiling | not quantified (true DFT skipped, real_compute=false); qualitative: EC:EMC standard stability ~4.3 V vs Li (literature) vs 4.2 V ceiling | medium | medium | charge ceiling fixed 4.2 V (parameter set) |
| Insufficient capacity/energy | thin/inactive mass dilution | ED 583.93 vs 500.94 (margin +16.6%) | high | low | implemented: thick electrodes, thin CC/sep |
| Current collector mechanical failure (manufacturing) | 6/4 um foils below common production gauge | no mechanical model | medium | medium (estimate) | flag for manufacturing review; 8/6 um acceptable alternative at ED 549 |
| Anode particle manufacturability | 1.0 um primary-particle-scale radius | no process model | low | medium (estimate) | fallback R4B (1.5 um anode, +0.0144 V) fully validated |

Conclusion: highest-risk items are manufacturing-class (thin foils, 1.0 um anode) — both with validated fallbacks; all simulation-quantifiable risks mitigated to PASS with positive margin. Complete FMEA incl. process/supplier N/A (beyond pure simulation boundary).

