## Case t5_r1_noceiling — closed, verdict: ACHIEVED

**Final design: R4A "MarginAnode1p0"** (Chen2020 NMC811|graphite + architecture overrides: electrodes 95.3/107.5 µm, width 2.37 m (area ×1.5), CC 6/4 µm, separator 8 µm, particles 1.5/1.0 µm, electrolyte transport σ 2.0 S/m / t⁺ 0.45 / D 4.5e-10 m²/s, h = 200 W/m²/K). All three contract criteria hold at **both** SPMe and DFN:

| Criterion | Result (DFN, primary) | SPMe cross-check | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| ED ≥ 500.94 Wh/kg | **583.93** (1042.10 Wh/L) | 583.46 | PASS (+16.6%) |
| 4C fast charge, no plating | 8.12 Ah in 1461 s to the 4.2 V ceiling (84.3% SOC), anode min **+0.0212 V** | +0.0270 V | PASS |
| T_max ≤ 60 °C | **320.36 K (47.2 °C)** | 320.44 K | PASS |

1C discharge: 9.6251 Ah, clean termination at 2.500 V (no 7200-s truncation). Validated fallback: R4B (+0.0144 V anode margin).

**Trajectory:** R1 baseline failed on all fronts (ED 400.75, 4C plated at −0.44 V) and bounded the architecture+formulation ceiling (~620–630 Wh/kg → objective reachable, no material escalation — also disabled by ablation). R2 localized the failure to empty-anode start-of-charge polarization. R3 fixed it (area ×1.5 + 1.5 µm particles → first full pass, +0.0162 V) and killed the N/P>1 branch on data. R4 polished ED and widened the margin → R4A.

**Closing artifacts:** log.jsonl now ends with the skip-honest `endorse` (real_compute=false) and the `final` entry (verdict achieved, full evidence chain and caveats). `deliverables/` holds all 7 categories as sources + PDF releases (design_spec, bom.xlsx, datasheet, calc.xlsx, dvpr, dfmea, delivery_index) plus `report.html`; `verify-deliverables: ALL PASS`. Manufacturing caveats (6/4 µm foils, 1.0 µm anode particles) are flagged in the spec/FMEA with validated fallbacks; cycle life and abuse tests honestly marked not simulated.
